Chromium 159.0.8154.28 -> 159.0.8154.45, for the 159.0.8154.28 tarball.

159.0.8154.45 is a tag on the 159 branch (refs/branch-heads/8154@{#1531}) that
has no source tarball (as of 2026-11-24: Google's lite bucket's newest 159 is .28,
chromium-linux-tarballs' is .13). It adds 505 branch commits to
159.0.8154.28 (#1026), the newest tag with a tarball, among them PGO/orderfile
rolls, translation updates, ChromeOS LKGM uprevs and VERSION increments. It adds,
among many CHECKs turned back into DCHECKs, Contextual Tasks ("Ask Google" entry
points, Omnibox fulfilment; the legacy ContextualTasksButton is deleted) and Cobrowse
tab tracking: Web Speech API's SpeechRecognitionResult timestamps on desktop,
ServiceWorker clients' worker script origin check, SimpleCache's doomed entries,
CacheStorage's empty puts, a use-after-free in optimization guide's SetInput()
callbacks, in FOR_DROP menu drag and drop, in ExplainSuggestion::AskGemini, in
ImageProcessor's get_pixels callback and in PermissionRequestManager's selectors,
WebPagePopup's initialization crashes, Blink's pseudo-elements no longer exposed as
Event.target, Blink keeping a parser-created script's provenance for CSP and pinning
parkable script text across threads, actor/WebMCP changes (ExecuteJsTool's console
capture, script tool token validation, JS dialogs intercepted during actuation),
MHTML only for allowed schemes, HLS disallowing every local scheme, SchemeHostPort
rejecting an empty host, serialization of cross-world references in their source
realm, the WebUI omnibox (no ".com" on Ctrl+Enter when the Ctrl was pressed elsewhere,
input language changes), the VariationsService HTTP fallback off by default, hybrid
post-quantum variations seed signatures with key rotation, deserialization of older
File System Access handles stored in IDB, cc's kSendEarlyFinalBeginMainFrame off by
default (security), the GPU process' OzoneImageBacking copies and a guard against
transfer buffer ID wraparound, the extension updater's start before the management
policy check, PageInfo's site data dialog WebContents guard, FedCM's ShowErrorDialog;
in the dependency rolls: ANGLE's D3D11 fixes (Windows only) and Vulkan's
rasterization-samples dynamic state off on Intel/mesa, Skia's Ganesh flush failures
abandoning the context, GrBufferAllocPool's overflow guard, LCD16 bounds hardening,
scissor restricted by dst-read bounds, predrawNotify on source-free saveLayer draws
and Graphite's depth reset, V8 15.9.128.16 to .34 (among them the debugger's
kNotAssigned assumptions, the compiler's control inputs on non-cell context
operations, TruncateFloat64ToInt64 for minus zero and 64-bit sources in mixed-width
move cycles, Turbolev's peeled-loop phis, Turboshaft's map-load folding, Maglev's
single-input phi untagging, Turbofan's DeadValue check in TryReuseDispatch, the
register allocator's multi-slot stack aliasing, the interpreter's optional-chain call
receiver, String::ToStdString's bound (also for Intl.Locale tags), the WebAssembly
streaming and code pointer table fixes) and Dawn's oversized strides in
Queue::WriteTexture, its OpenGL texture image units limit on PowerVR and Metal's
extractBits polyfill (plus its DXC pin, DEPS only).

Generated from the upstream diffs between the tags: chromium/src
refs/tags/159.0.8154.28..refs/tags/159.0.8154.45 and the dependencies whose
DEPS revision changed (ANGLE b49535777c51..4dd34493f8a2, Skia
458e1f1ab81e..b809e72312b0, V8 ff20afeabcd5..90a5172104e6, Dawn
16b69da1f131..e6ee1e531926), as served by Gitiles, with scripts/chromium-delta.
The other dependencies' DEPS revisions don't change (the .28 tarball has them).

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations (but en-GB), CI configuration, PGO/orderfile pointers, submodule
pointer updates, DEPS. GN files (*.gn, *.gni) are kept even for tests and other
platforms: gn gen reads test targets' BUILD.gn too.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime}, gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h,
skia/ext/skia_commit_hash.h, gpu/webgpu/DAWN_VERSION and
gpu/webgpu/dawn_commit_hash.h; commit
14fa8421e6009e9080f6111fc97664d7c89aaa37, refs/branch-heads/8154@{#1531}).
build/util/MINIBRANCH doesn't change.

Checked: applies to the 159.0.8154.28 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
159.0.8154.45; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag (or its dependency's DEPS revision); it adds 7 files and deletes
4; the 159.0.8154.28 tarball's non-git files are all classified
(tarball-generated.py with generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

